{{Quote|It's a hit!|Naytaan during the Battle of Yavin|<ref name="Episode 4">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
'''Nozzo Naytaan''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Rebel pilot]] and [[lieutenant]]<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> who served in the [[Galactic Civil War]]. A member of [[Red Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Red Squadron]], he flew in the [[Battle of Scarif]] with the [[callsign]] of [[Red Nine]]. Both from [[Corellia]], Naytaan and [[Lieutenant]] [[Attico Wred]], a fellow [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] [[pilot]] who flew with [[Green Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Green Squadron]] as [[Green Four]], had a friendly rivalry.<ref name="SWROUVG" /> Just [[Standard day|days]] after the Battle of Scarif, Naytaan was [[Death|killed]] during the [[Battle of Yavin]].<ref name="Duty Roster" />

During the [[Imperialization]] of the [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]], Naytaan was a test pilot for the company. After learning that he would be assigned to test [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighters]] for the [[Galactic Empire]], Naytaan fled and joined the Rebellion.<ref name="SWROUVG" />

At some point prior to [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|IV|1}}</ref> Naytaan was scheduled Shift Cycle 2 of an X-wing flight patrol mission accompanying fellow pilots [[Cadet|Cdt.]] [[Harb Binli]] ([[Red Seven]]) and [[Pedrin Gaul]] ([[Red Five]]). Their mission was to route from [[Yavin Prime|Yavin]] to [[Gordian Reach|Gordian]] Trace Relays, perform a flyby of surrounding space, then after verifying visual and sensor all clear, perform close uplink of passive relay recordings.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:AtticoWredHelmet-SW100Objects.png|thumb|right|200px|Nozzo Naytaan's flight helmet was similar to Attico Wred's helmet]]
Naytaan's voice is heard in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]. His two lines of dialogue, "Red Nine standing by" and "It's a hit!" were both spoken over the comm systems of his X-wing starfighter, although his second line wasn't associated with his character until 2008. He was identified as Red Nine at the Battle of Scarif by ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''. In [[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story|Star Wars: Rogue One]], Nozzo Naytaan is portrayed by [[Frank Stone]]. The short story "[[Duty Roster]]" later re-canonized Nozzo's participation in the Battle of Yavin.

In [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]], Naytaan was stated to be born on [[Regellia]]. In [[canon]], ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'' changed his homeworld to [[Corellia]].

Naytaan's helmet is similar to the design of [[Attico Wred]]'s in the film. They both match the design of [[Luke Skywalker/Legends|Luke Skywalker's]] blast shield helmet in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''A New Hope'']] and [[Dorovio Bold/Legends|Dorovio Bold's]] helmet in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Return of the Jedi'']],<ref name="Costumes">''[[Star Wars Costumes: The Original Trilogy]]''</ref> as well [[Darnell Reggs]]' from the Legends video game [[Star Wars: Rebel Assault II: The Hidden Empire|''Rebel Assault II: The Hidden Empire'']].

